<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  MandrakeJawaXenotype.xml                   Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-14
  ============================================================================

  OWNER'S RULING, 2026-08-14: "the xenotype MandrakeJawa is the ONLY Jawa
  xenotype active anymore."

  WHERE THE GENES CAME FROM
  =========================
  Transcribed from the owner's own custom xenotype, saved in the game's editor:
      C:\Users\Mandrake\AppData\LocalLow\Ludeon Studios\RimWorld by Ludeon Studios\Xenotypes\MandrakeJawa.xtp
  A copy is committed at `src/Jawa/ideoligion/MandrakeJawa.xtp` so the source of
  this def cannot be lost with the AppData folder.

  🔴 WHY A DEF AND NOT JUST THE .xtp
  ==================================
  A `.xtp` is a saved *custom* xenotype: it is loaded by the pawn editor at game
  start and it is NOT a def. Nothing can reference it — `PawnKindDef.xenotypeSet`
  takes XenotypeDefs. So the owner's request for a colonist pawnkind carrying
  this xenotype is only satisfiable by promoting the .xtp into a real def, which
  is what this file does. The two must be kept in step by hand; if the owner
  edits the .xtp in game, re-transcribe.

  GENES: 38. The first 35 are the .xtp's own order, transcribed verbatim.
  `inheritable` True matches the .xtp, so children of two Jawa are Jawa.

  🔴 THE DEF AND THE .xtp NOW DIFFER BY EXACTLY THREE GENES, ON PURPOSE
  ====================================================================
  `AptitudeTerrible_Plants` is the 36th, added 2026-08-21 (JAWA_CANNOT_FARM_GENE_1);
  `RimMandrake_Jawa_MiningDisabled` is the 37th, added 2026-08-22
  (JAWA_CANNOT_DIG_GENE_1); and `SEX_AlwaysAphrodor` is the 38th, added 2026-08-22 on
  the owner's description of the clan as a "single-gender-egg-layer-either-impregnate-
  the-other variety" - see the long note beside it below for why the ovipositor alone
  did not deliver that. All three are on the owner's rulings. None is in
  `MandrakeJawa.xtp` and none must be
  put there: the .xtp is the owner's saved editor artifact and a record of what
  he built by hand, and the repo copy is byte-identical to the live one under
  `LocalLow\Xenotypes\`. Both should stay that way.
  ⛔ THIS PARAGRAPH REPLACES "the two must be kept in step by hand." They are
  deliberately NOT in step. If the owner edits the .xtp in game and someone
  re-transcribes it over this def, ALL THREE ARE SILENTLY LOST - the def still
  loads, every Jawa still generates, and the only symptoms are a clan that farms
  happily, digs its own ore, and quietly reverts to two ordinary sexes.
  Re-add all three after any re-transcribe.

  `iconPath` is Outer Rim's Jawa icon, copied into this mod with the rest of
  the species art. Credit for it is Neronix17's.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <XenotypeDef>
    <defName>MandrakeJawa</defName>
    <label>Jawa</label>
    <description>The clan aboard the Kolyska. Small, hooded, ink-black of skin and huge of eye, bred narrow by a desert that never turns from the sun. They see in the dark, they carry the scent of their own kind, they lay eggs rather than bear young, and every one of them is male. They are frail, sour-stomached and quick to flinch — and they will strip a wreck to its frame and make it run again.</description>
    <descriptionShort>Small hooded desert scavengers with huge glowing eyes, dark vision and an unmatched instinct for salvage.</descriptionShort>
    <iconPath>RimMandrakeSW/OR/OuterRim/XenotypeIcons/Xenotype_Jawa</iconPath>
    <inheritable>true</inheritable>
    <!-- The player's own clan. It should not turn up as unaffiliated filler or
         as generic raider stock; the indigenous tribes get it through their own
         FactionDef and PawnKindDefs, not through random generation. -->
    <!-- 0 keeps Jawa out of the random-wanderer pool. The factions that should
         field them name the xenotype explicitly in their own xenotypeSet, so
         this costs nothing and stops stray Jawa arriving as event pawns. -->
    <factionlessGenerationWeight>0</factionlessGenerationWeight>
    <!-- 🔴 WAS `false`, AND THAT WAS A DEFECT. It is not in the owner's .xtp;
         that file carries only `name` and `inheritable`, so it was invented
         when this def was written. `false` bars the xenotype from COMBAT pawn
         generation, and `Jawa_IndigenousTribes` has a Combat group whose every
         option (Jawa_Tribal_Scavenger / _Slinger / _Elder) forces MandrakeJawa.
         A Jawa faction that cannot generate a fighter is a faction that cannot
         raid. Every vanilla faction xenotype (Neanderthal, Hussar, Impid)
         ships `true`. -->
    <canGenerateAsCombatant>true</canGenerateAsCombatant>
    <combatPowerFactor>0.85</combatPowerFactor>
    <!-- Jawa names, not colonist names. The rule pack and its word lists are
         this mod's, copied from Star Wars Xenotypes and renamed, so this holds
         with every donor switched off. -->
    <nameMaker>RimMandrake_KoTOR_NamerJawa</nameMaker>
    <genes>
      <!-- frame and constitution -->
      <li>RimMandrake_BodySizeGene_smaller</li>
      <li>StrongStomach</li>
      <li>AG_UnderdevelopedTeeth</li>
      <li>AG_SurvivalInstinct_High</li>
      <li>AG_TableResistance</li>
      <li>WoundHealing_Slow</li>
      <li>Superclotting</li>
      <li>AG_Stinky</li>
      <li>AG_FrailSkin</li>
      <li>Mood_Pessimist</li>
      <li>MinTemp_SmallIncrease</li>
      <li>MaxTemp_LargeIncrease</li>
      <li>MeleeDamage_Weak</li>
      <li>RimMandrake_Jawa_Skittish</li>
      <li>Pain_Extra</li>
      <!-- reproduction: egg-laying, early maturity, short gestation -->
      <li>BS_EarlyMaturity</li>
      <li>VRE_ShortPregnancy</li>
      <!-- 🔴 OWNER, 2026-08-22: the Jawa are a "single-gender-egg-layer-either-impregnate-
           the-other variety". THAT TAKES TWO GENES AND ONLY ONE WAS HERE.
           Read out of the decompiled Intimacy - Gender Works assembly, not inferred:

           `GenderUtilities.ApplyReproductives` walks a pawn's ACTIVE genes and ORs the
           flags from each `GenderWorksModExtension`. Crucially, the `SEX_Ovipositor`
           extension sets only `femaleReproductiveReplacement` - it does NOT set the
           "a gene decided this" flag. So with the ovipositor ALONE that flag stays false,
           `GetGenderBasedReproductivesForPawn` runs, and every Jawa falls back to the
           gender default: males become phallors and females become gestors.
           ⇒ 🔴 AND BECAUSE `Outland_AllMale` IS ALSO ON THIS LIST, THE GENDER DEFAULT
           MADE **EVERY** JAWA A PHALLOR. Not half - all of them. The ovipositor gene was
           doing nothing for a single member of the species, because its own description
           is "GESTOR OR APHRODOR carriers of this gene will be born with an ovipositor"
           and there were no gestors and no aphrodors. The clan was an all-male species
           that could not reproduce at all with itself and carried an inert egg gene.
           ⚠️ A correction to my own first note here, which said "half of them" - that was
           written before I checked `Outland_AllMale`, and it understated the defect.

           `SEX_AlwaysAphrodor` gives BOTH organs to every carrier regardless of gender,
           and the ovipositor then replaces the female one. So a Jawa has a phallus and an
           ovipositor: any Jawa can impregnate any other Jawa, and whichever was
           impregnated lays an egg. That is the owner's sentence, mechanically.
           🔑 It is gender-BLIND, not gender-changing, and that is what makes it compose
           with `Outland_AllMale` instead of fighting it. Every Jawa stays male - the
           owner's own build, and the single-gender half of his description - while the
           reproductive class stops following gender at all. Nothing here touches how a
           Jawa looks; `Hair_BaldOnly` and `Beard_NoBeardOnly` above still do that.

           ⚠️ CONCEPTION IS DECIDED BY ORGANS AND NEVER BY GENDER once this mod is loaded:
           its `PregnancyUtility.CanEverProduceChild` prefix replaces the vanilla method
           outright and asks only whether one partner has a male organ and the other a
           female one. Sexuality traits are untouched and still decide who WANTS to pair.

           ⛔ NOT `SEX_Meiosis`. It reads like the same idea and is the opposite one:
           parthenogenesis, self-impregnation, and its own effect description says it
           "prevents regular conception". It would replace pairing rather than open it up.
           ⛔ NOT `SEX_AlwaysGestor` or `SEX_AlwaysPhallor` either - those force ONE class
           on every member of the species, males included, because the flags OR and there
           is no per-gender branch anywhere in that loop. -->
      <li>SEX_AlwaysAphrodor</li>
      <li>SEX_Ovipositor</li>
      <!-- appearance -->
      <li>Hair_BaldOnly</li>
      <li>Beard_NoBeardOnly</li>
      <li>Body_Standard</li>
      <li>Skin_InkBlack</li>
      <li>RimMandrake_Eyes_HugeYellow</li>
      <li>RimMandrake_Jawa_Eyes_HugeOrange</li>
      <li>RimMandrake_Jawa_Eyes_HugeAmber</li>
      <li>Outland_Blood_Gray</li>
      <li>RimMandrake_Jawa_Head_Plain</li>
      <!-- the ones that carry the fiction -->
      <li>DarkVision</li>
      <li>Outland_FamiliarScent</li>
      <li>Outland_Evasive</li>
      <li>Outland_AllMale</li>
      <!-- aptitudes: they build, they make, they haggle - and they do not farm -->
      <li>AptitudeStrong_Construction</li>
      <li>AptitudeStrong_Crafting</li>
      <li>AptitudeStrong_Social</li>
      <!-- 🔴 OWNER, 2026-08-21: "We should simply add a line that Jawa genetics has a
           disability toward farming." This replaced a ScenPart designator rule plus a
           14-entry Rule_DisallowBuilding list, and it is the better mechanism as well as
           the smaller one: a scenario rule binds the PLAYER'S UI on one save, a gene binds
           the PAWN - so it reaches enemy Jawa factions too, survives into any save, and
           needs no list that decays every time a furniture mod is added.
           ⚠️ AN APTITUDE, NOT `disabledWorkTags`, and the owner ruled that fork explicitly.
           There is no `Growing`-only WorkTag - only `PlantWork`, which covers PlantCutting
           as well - so disabling it would also stop a Jawa harvesting, cutting wild plants
           and CHOPPING TREES. No wood, on a scavenger clan. -8 makes them bad at farming
           and leaves the axe in their hands. -->
      <li>AptitudeTerrible_Plants</li>
      <!-- 🔴 OWNER: "they should not be able to mine ore, though some other races still
           can. And the mining laser should be able to do this very well."
           ⚠️ A HARD DISABLE HERE AND A SOFT APTITUDE ABOVE, and that is not an
           inconsistency - the WorkTags enum is not symmetrical. `PlantWork` is the only
           plant tag and drags `PlantCutting`, so disabling it would cost the clan its
           firewood; `Mining` covers the Mining work type and nothing else.
           🔑 The deep drill goes with it, deliberately - vanilla's `Drill` WorkGiver is
           `workType Mining`. The drill TURRET still works because
           DRILLTURRET_IS_A_SHOOTING_JOB_1 moved it to `Hunting`, which also means this
           design depends on Jawa being capable of VIOLENT work. No gene in this list
           disables a work tag; keep it that way or the turret silently dies. -->
      <li>RimMandrake_Jawa_MiningDisabled</li>
      <li>VRE_Curiosity_Social</li>
    </genes>
  </XenotypeDef>

</Defs>
